
  ╭─────────────────────────────────────────── How to use ───────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │                                                                                                  │
  │  [1mThemes[0m are an easy way to style a rich-click CLI.                                               │
  │                                                                                                  │
  │  As an end-user of CLIs, you can set the [1;34mRICH_CLICK_THEME=[0m env var to style all rich-click CLIs  │
  │  you use.                                                                                        │
  │                                                                                                  │
  │  As a developer, you can add a theme to your CLI with one line of code:                          │
  │  [1;32m@click.rich_config({'theme': 'name'})[0m.                                                          │
  │                                                                                                  │
  │  Themes consist of [1mColor Palettes[0m and [1mFormats[0m, which can be mixed and matched: The name of a     │
  │  full theme has the following schema: [31m{color_palette}-{format}[0m.                                  │
  │                                                                                                  │
  │  For example, the [1mforest-slim[0m theme uses the [1mforest[0m color palette and the [1mslim[0m format.           │
  │                                                                                                  │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
